# ResetSignal configs build a field-local async reset domain via the
# Clocks package on BOTH sides (blind ref and generator instantiate an
# identical MakeResetA -> SyncResetA subtree). Those two bsc library
# primitives must be read in so Yosys can flatten through the reset
# domain rather than treating it as a black box; the test driver copies
# them from bsc's Verilog library dir. async2sync (already in the shared
# boilerplate below) handles the async-reset FFs for equiv_induct.
read_verilog MakeResetA.v
read_verilog SyncResetA.v
read_verilog mkResetSignalHigh.v
read_verilog gold_top.v
read_verilog testcsrreg_reg0_field0.v
read_verilog gate_top.v

rename gold_top gold
rename gate_top gate

proc
memory
flatten gold
flatten gate
delete mkResetSignalHigh
delete testcsrreg_reg0_field0

equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
prep
async2sync
equiv_induct
equiv_status -assert
